School foundation program interim budget 25LSO-0118, 1.0
authority.
FISCAL NOTE
This fiscal impact is indeterminable.
This bill prohibits the Governor from increasing legislative appropriations from
the Public School Foundation Program Account (SFP) except to ensure sufficient
funds are available to fund the foundation program amount as defined by W.S. 21-
13-101(a)(v) for each school district (i.e., the Wyoming education resource block
grant funding model and other amounts made available to school districts to comply
with providing the K-12 educational program).
Under current law, W.S. 9-2-1005(b)(ii), the Governor has the authority to revise,
change, redistribute or increase legislative appropriations from the SFP, if in his
opinion a public welfare emergency exists, agency program requirements have
significantly changed, or if there are unanticipated revenues that become available.
